REFERENCE   6  (bases 1 to 5378)
  AUTHORS   Wu,X., Lim,Z.F., Li,Z., Gu,L., Ma,W., Zhou,Q., Su,H., Wang,X.,
            Yang,X. and Zhang,Z.
  TITLE     NORAD Expression Is Associated with Adverse Prognosis in Esophageal
            Squamous Cell Carcinoma
  JOURNAL   Oncol Res Treat 40 (6), 370-374 (2017)
   PUBMED   28482344
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Our data indicate that increased NORAD expression might
            serve as a novel molecular predictor of poor prognosis in ESCC
            patients and maybe a potential target for diagnosis and gene
            therapy.
            Erratum:[Oncol Res Treat. 2017;40(7-8):451. doi: 10.1159/000477509.
            PMID: 28768273]
REFERENCE   7  (bases 1 to 5378)
  AUTHORS   Tichon,A., Gil,N., Lubelsky,Y., Havkin Solomon,T., Lemze,D.,
            Itzkovitz,S., Stern-Ginossar,N. and Ulitsky,I.
  TITLE     A conserved abundant cytoplasmic long noncoding RNA modulates
            repression by Pumilio proteins in human cells
  JOURNAL   Nat Commun 7, 12209 (2016)
   PUBMED   27406171
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Through binding to PUM1 and PUM2, NORAD modulates the mRNA
            levels of their targets, which are enriched for genes involved in
            chromosome segregation during cell division. Our results suggest
            that some cytoplasmic lncRNAs function by modulating the activities
            of RNA-binding proteins, an activity which positions them at key
            junctions of cellular signalling pathways.
REFERENCE   8  (bases 1 to 5378)
  AUTHORS   Ventura,A.
  TITLE     NORAD: Defender of the Genome
  JOURNAL   Trends Genet 32 (7), 390-392 (2016)
   PUBMED   27157388
  REMARK    GeneRIF: A recent paper by the Mendell group identifies NORAD, a
            novel lncRNA that is regulated in response to DNA damage and plays
            a key role in maintaining genome integrity by modulating the
            activity the RNA binding proteins PUM2 and PUM1.
            Review article
REFERENCE   9  (bases 1 to 5378)
  AUTHORS   Liu,H., Li,J., Koirala,P., Ding,X., Chen,B., Wang,Y., Wang,Z.,
            Wang,C., Zhang,X. and Mo,Y.Y.
  TITLE     Long non-coding RNAs as prognostic markers in human breast cancer
  JOURNAL   Oncotarget 7 (15), 20584-20596 (2016)
   PUBMED   26942882
  REMARK    GeneRIF: High LINC00657 expression is associated with breast
            cancer.
REFERENCE   10 (bases 1 to 5378)
  AUTHORS   Lee,S., Kopp,F., Chang,T.C., Sataluri,A., Chen,B., Sivakumar,S.,
            Yu,H., Xie,Y. and Mendell,J.T.
  TITLE     Noncoding RNA NORAD Regulates Genomic Stability by Sequestering
            PUMILIO Proteins
  JOURNAL   Cell 164 (1-2), 69-80 (2016)
   PUBMED   26724866
  REMARK    GeneRIF: NORAD is highly conserved and abundant, with expression
            levels of approximately 500-1,000 copies per cell. Remarkably,
            inactivation of NORAD triggers dramatic aneuploidy in previously
            karyotypically stable cell lines. NORAD maintains genomic stability
            by sequestering PUMILIO proteins, which repress the stability and
            translation of mRNAs to which they bind.
